wave.scope:
Options sensitivity [0,1e6] and basefreq [2,1e6], plain decimals. Refuse enable and commands. Pinned 'dblp'.
- stream() keeps per-channel low1, low2 and inz, zero-initialised.
- Mirror the exact double expression order with no fusion:
  - wc = basefreq/sample_rate per frame;
  - bandz = low2z - low1z; wd = wc + sens*|bandz|;
  - g = fmin(1, wd*(5.9948827 + wd*(-11.969296 + wd*15.959062)));
  - low1 = low1z + g*(0.5*(x+inz) - low1z);
  - low2 = low2z + g*(0.5*(low1+low1z) - low2z); inz = x.
- reserve(): one frame plus 3 doubles per channel.

waveRules:
Each branch must contain:
- the descriptor or format module;
- the registry line(s);
- tests/unit/<...>.test.ts;
- tests/differential/<...>.test.ts, generating inputs in the test and running native at test time, with no committed native goldens;
- docs/contributing/<...>.md with syntax, supported vs refused forms, determinism and arithmetic profile, evidence counts, scoped test contracts (file, exact test title, scope), and the sandbox's ffmpeg sha256 and `cc --version`;
- a NOTICE-<NAME> provenance file citing the pinned commit 946fcce0.

Before pushing, run:
- the branch's unit and differential files (differential with --maxWorkers=1);
- tests/unit/audio-filter-registry.test.ts and tests/unit/audio-filter-registry-extension.test.ts (audio), or tests/unit/video-operator-registry.test.ts (video);
- npm run typecheck, npm run lint and npm run boundaries.
Do not run the full `npm test` or `npm run check`: they need edge-flac.wasm, which cannot be fetched in the sandbox. Each differential file should finish in about 3 minutes on 4 vCPUs, so batch native calls and keep the matrices bounded.

After every 10 merges run typecheck and the three registry unit tests. After the last merge:
- run all 40 differential files on a Linux x86_64 host;
- run `npm run check` plus the FLAC integration and workers suites on the macOS host that has edge-flac.wasm (the linux-gated float cases skip there);
- then record evidence in compat/*.json, development-status.md and the registry docs in one validation commit.
